An unordered backlog: what is still to do, plus the negative findings that
would otherwise be paid for twice. Completed work is not logged here -
its history lives in docs/plans/, docs/design/, and git.

The ranked survey behind the dbarts-capability items - what the seam is,
what each costs, and which need dbarts to grow first - is
docs/design/dbarts-capability-adoption.md. An item graduates to its own
docs/plans/<item>.md when it is picked up.

items
  callback-estimators: TABLED with its consumer (bartCause) 2026-07-16.
    The design and measurements are complete in
    docs/plans/callback-estimators.md (per-draw reducing callbacks
    store draws x estimators instead of n x draws surfaces; prototype
    +1.1 percent wall, bitwise ate; the stan4bart-side contract
    refinements - assembled response-scale ev to the callback, warmup
    gating, documenting the seam - are consumer-gated and land with
    adoption).
  ordinal-outcomes: ordered-categorical responses via dbarts's
    cumulative probit. Structurally the existing binary path -
    getLatents into the parametric response, cutpoints drawn
    engine-side. Cheapest genuinely new family, and multilevel ordinal
    is a core audience need.
  log-lik-loo: surface dbarts_results.logLikelihood (per-observation,
    already computed for gaussian/binary/aft; the BART offset is the
    parametric mean, so what it reports is the joint conditional
    likelihood) as a log_lik extract type plus loo/waic methods.
    Storage opt-in, same discipline as store=.
  dbarts-passthroughs: wire, document, and test the features that
    dbarts-spec-adoption only made REACHABLE - storage="single", sparse
    columns, warm starts, and the substantive use of monotone and
    interactions()/blocks() (the last is also the cheap R-side
    mitigation of the forest-ranef confounding dbarts investigated and
    declined to fix in the engine). missing="incorporate" (MIA on
    BART-only covariates) is the one item here that is NOT a knob:
    dbartsSpec does not take it, it is a dbartsData argument, and the
    lme4 ingestion in lme4_functions.R drops NA rows through
    model.frame's na.action before dbartsData ever sees them and again
    through the union na.action.all. Reaching it means teaching the
    ingestion to keep NA rows for the bart frame alone while the fixed
    and random frames stay complete - an arc, not a forwarded name.
  per-observation-variance: robust-t residuals and a heteroscedastic
    variance forest, as ONE arc - both need per-observation precision
    to flow BART -> parametric, reversing today's scalar setSigma
    direction. Blocked on dbarts appending a working-weights/variance
    field to dbarts_results (additive, MINOR bump); this side then sets
    the parametric weights per iteration, which the Eigen model already
    carries but fixes at construction. dbarts-gated.
  aft-frailty: multilevel accelerated-failure-time survival.
    dbartsSpec(family = "aft", survival = ) already builds the
    specification; the open question is whether the imputed censored
    response is reachable through getLatents. Check that first - if it
    is, the rest is wiring, and multilevel survival is an unoccupied
    niche.
  multilevel-bcf: the two-forest (prognostic + treatment) BCF
    parameterization under random effects - the largest research payoff
    here, and what bartCause would consume. Needs a new dbarts.h entry
    point: BCF is built by its own path inside dbarts and is not
    exposed through the flat C API at all. decision-gated.
  vendored-headers: when syncing a file from dbarts, copy it and
    rewrite external/ -> ext/ (this package names that directory ext,
    dbarts names it external); that one line is the only permitted
    divergence, and vendor only what is reached from this package's own
    sources. As of 412df11 the vendored set is ext/Rinternals.h,
    rc/{bounds,util}.h, rc_{bounds,util}.c - all byte-identical to
    dbarts modulo that rewrite - plus misc/stddef.h, which is the one
    deliberate exception: it omits upstream's misc_index_t, a dbarts
    kernel type this package does not use. Do NOT vendor upstream's
    external/{random,stats}.h or ext/{io,R}.h; io.h declares
    ext_printMessage/ext_throwError/ext_issueWarning, which live in
    dbarts's external.a, a library this package does not link, so the
    header is unusable here rather than merely unused. Do NOT
    re-vendor misc/intrinsic.h or the AX_EXT configure machinery
    deleted with the radix tree - a dbarts source wanting intrinsic.h
    also wants upstream's AX_COMPILER_EXT configure side, and the two
    must move together, since the macro names look cosmetic and are not
    (COMPILER_SUPPORTS_SSE2 asks whether the compiler accepts -msse2;
    the old HAVE_SSE2 asked whether the build host's cpuid reported
    it).
  perf-measurement: two traps, kept because both were expensive to find
    and neither leaves a trace once the wrong number is written down.
    (1) Per-iteration cost must be differenced between two fits IN ONE
    WARM PROCESS. Differencing two cold subprocesses charges the long
    run for page-in on the sample-storage arrays, a cost that scales
    with iter and reads back as compute. The error is not a constant
    offset - it grows with the per-draw storage footprint, so it does
    not cancel across commits: it reported 700 us/iter on 174b369
    against a warm truth of 163, and 137 on 3e2036b against 144. That
    gradient was the whole of a "4x per-iteration speedup" chased
    across 174b369..3e2036b, where cost is in fact flat; no stan4bart
    or dbarts commit in that window moved it. Fixed in bench-perf.R at
    412df11, whose comment carries the numbers.
    (2) Quiet is top's INSTANTANEOUS idle sample. Load average and ps
    %CPU both decay, so they read a just-finished benchmark as load and
    a genuinely idle machine as busy.
    (3) Compare two samplers only with dbarts pinned to ONE version.
    Neither side can run against both - the pre-merge line predates the
    parsePriors and structSize changes 1.0-0 requires - so a rebuild of
    the older side against the older dbarts is the only honest pairing.
    This is how NEWS.md's 53-95x was derived; see the cb809b1 MANIFEST
    row.
  release: stan4bart 0.0-14, in lockstep with dbarts 1.0-0. dbarts
    ships first; its TODO owns the ordered procedure. LAST.
